message: Please cite the paper; this repository supplies its source.
type: software
title: "Group algebras that are domains but embed in no division ring"
version: 1.0.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24202768"
date-released: '2026-11-13'
license: [CC-BY-4.0, MIT, Apache-2.0]
authors: [{"family-names": "Mghirbi", "given-names": "Nidhal", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6534-1118"}, {"family-names": "Douglas", "given-names": "Seth", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"}]
keywords: ["group algebras", "division rings", "unique product groups", "diffuse groups", "hyperbolic groups", "Kourovka Notebook", "Malcev embedding problem"]
abstract: "For every prime p, we construct a finitely presented, torsion-free, word-hyperbolic diffuse group Γ_p whose group algebra is a domain over every field and embeds in no division ring over any field of characteristic p. A marked-line complex supplies a universal finite-field rank ceiling. We glue finitely many copies of its group to a free vertex group, using every permutation of a free basis array; a noncommutative permutation-averaging lemma contradicts that ceiling. We prove concentration of the line subgroups by separate geometric cone attachments and a free-product calculation for punctured CAT(0) complexes. Acylindrical combination gives hyperbolicity, and Bowditch's graph-of-groups theorem gives diffuseness. We also give a shorter retractive construction using shear attachments with bi-orderable kernel, together with its general rank-forcing principle. These examples answer Kourovka Problem 1.5 for group algebras over fields of every positive characteristic. The integral and characteristic-zero versions, and Mal'cev's problem, remain open."
